-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- derivations: one family over the rule table
-- A rule is its data (RData), its conclusion (concl), its premises (premJ: each a role and a judgment) and
-- the tags it concludes at (kallows). Der is the family at tag any, the normal and neutral forms NN at nf and
-- ne; a premise's tag is its role's tag at the conclusion's (rtag). One recursion over the family (d-fold)
-- serves embed, renaming and the fundamental lemma: each is an algebra, one clause per rule's meaning.
data Tag = t-ne | t-nf | t-any
